<title>USA: United Auto Group sees $2 bln sales in 1997.</title>
<headline>United Auto Group sees $2 bln sales in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Auto Group Inc said Wednesday that it plans to post $2 billion in sales for 1997 and $4 billion in sales by 2000.</p>
<p>The company said Chairman Carl Spielvogel offered that projection in addressing a Smith Barney conference on emerging growth stocks.</p>
<p>United Auto acquires, consolidates and operates franchised dealerships and related businesses.</p>
<p>For the first nine months of the 1996 fiscal year, the company has posted net income of $16.4 million, or $0.92 per share, on sales of $1.23 billion.</p>
</text>
